      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The village’s name comes from the Biblical Land of Goshen, reflecting early settlers’ hopes for fertile soil.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goshen%2C_New_York",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Between Chicago and Jersey City, Erie Railroad’s Erie Limited and Lake Cities stopped at Goshen’s station through the 1950s.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goshen%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Goshen Public Library’s Local History Room, on the second floor of 366 Main Street, offers digitized newspapers and a microfilm machine for the Goshen Independent Republican.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
